  "headline": "Ontario to import 600 megawatts of electricity from New York this winter",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Ontario has signed a contract to import 600 megawatts of electricity from New York state this winter to offset unspecified facility maintenance, according to the Independent Electricity System Operator. The agreement follows a period weeks prior when Ontario Premier Doug Ford threatened to cut off electricity exports to the U.S. as retaliation in an ongoing trade war."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "Sudanese army claims dozens of RSF fighters killed in Nyala attacks",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "The Sudanese army says it killed dozens of fighters from the Rapid Support Forces (RSF) during a series of air attacks on October 16, 2026, in Nyala, the capital of South Darfur state. In a statement, the army identified its targets as RSF positions and command centres in the city, which serves as the seat of the paramilitary group’s self-declared administration. The RSF has not confirmed or denied whether separate attacks killed its fighters or destroyed its command centres. Al Jazeera reporter Almigdad Alruhaid reported from Khartoum on Saturday that fighting between the army and the RSF has intensified. Additionally, a Sudanese government source told Al Jazeera that the RSF carried out drone attacks on mining sites in South Kordofan as exchanges of fire intensified in many parts of Sudan over a 24-hour period."
    },
    {
      "text": "The RSF has accused the Sudanese army of killing 30 civilians, including 17 women and five children, during a drone attack on a busy livestock market in Nyala on October 16, 2026. The human rights group Emergency Lawyers also stated on X that a market in Nyala was hit on that date by a drone “affiliated” with the Sudanese army. The army has repeatedly used drones to target the Darfur region in western Sudan in an effort to retake territory held by the RSF. Earlier this month, Sudanese military chief Abdel Fattah al-Burhan promised to seize all territory under RSF control. The Sudanese civil war, which began in 2023, has killed tens of thousands of people, and the United Nations has described the situation as the world’s worst humanitarian crisis."
    }
  ]
}
